        <item>
            <title>3.26.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:55:23 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>240</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.26.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's New in 3.26.0</h2><ul></ul><p><strong>New</strong></p><ul><li>Zush can add a file's AI description to its Spotlight comment, so Spotlight finds files by what's in them. Turn on Make files searchable in Spotlight. Undo puts back the comment the file had before.</li><li>In the version downloaded from zushapp.com, the description also shows as the file's comment in Finder's Get Info window once you allow Zush to control Finder.</li><li>Rename rules and folder rules can now be up to 5,000 characters.</li></ul><p><strong>Improved</strong></p><ul><li>AI names keep useful details from the original file name, such as a part, chapter or episode number, a version, a status like final or signed, and the account a file was saved from.</li><li>If you close the template editor with unsaved changes, Zush asks whether to save them.</li><li>If a template or the Smart Rename settings can't be saved, Zush says so and keeps your changes.</li><li>The rename rules field explains that its rules apply to every file the template renames.</li></ul><p><strong>Fixed</strong></p><ul><li>Office documents saved in the newer format but named .xls or .ppt are now read correctly.</li><li>Folder monitoring no longer touches files inside packages such as .xcarchive.</li><li>When a folder that sorting planned to create already exists, the files wait for a new plan instead of failing.</li></ul>
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://zushapp.com/releases/Zush-3.26.0.dmg" length="20570964" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="QkLTgpRxRYjT2zhSUGXhB7E+rMbUe7MLsfz7xMkWlfYnpfDTyg0E9+6oyJ1iWCGV94pixMS4+dYb9XjQ1yqCCw=="/>
